  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the compound 23132-87, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N acts as a target for several molecules, including A704 and LC4-1, which in turn target a shared intermediate, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This intermediate is a known target of 23132-87, reinforcing a potential pathway where Mollicellin N influences the activity of this compound. The consistent presence of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a common intermediate across different targets suggests a functional link between Mollicellin N and 23132-87, possibly through the modulation of this intermediate. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Mollicellin N modulates the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn affects 23132-87. The evidence supports a mechanism involving a shared intermediate, with Mollicellin N acting as a regulator of this intermediate's activity, thereby influencing 23132-87.",
